  "description": "A delicate, not-too-sweet ricotta-flavored ice cream ripe for scooping onto pie and customizing with your favorite add-ins.",
  "notes": "Total time, including resting: 4 hr 50 min.\n\nOptional or for serving: Optional mix-ins (see note)\n\nNotes: Look for fresh, finely grained ricotta that doesn't skimp on fat. See our taste test on the best storebought ricotta here; this ice cream was made with Sorrento.\nCorn syrup gives the ice cream a smooth, easy-to-scoop, glossy texture despite its relatively low fat content. Other liquid sugars like agave nectar or honey can't be substituted without altering the recipe.\nA teaspoon or two of lemon, orange, or grapefruit zest would be a nice addition, as would dark chocolate or cocoa nibs, candied orange peel and chopped pistachio, or a drizzle of honey.",
